  "body": "Instagram checkpoint discovery captures complete GitHub comparison responses even though it only needs ancestry status. Large unrelated patches can exhaust the subprocess output buffer and block discovery of an otherwise valid encrypted checkpoint.\n\nProject comparison, workflow-run, and artifact responses inside `gh` before bounded capture. Preserve every field used for provenance, identity, expiry, and successful-producer validation; retain pagination, timeout and fail-closed behavior. The existing branch commit and author are preserved.\n\nValidation on exact head `40034a31e32ca7d1dbbf6dae67efda8eef982586`: `node --test scripts/__tests__/instagram-token-workflows.test.mjs` passed 90/90; `git diff --check HEAD^ HEAD` passed. Tests include output projection, retained provenance/expiry fields, and redaction on execution/JSON failures. No token lifecycle workflow, credential rotation, or deployment was manually triggered. Protected merge remains pending independent approval and applicable hosted checks.\n",
  "created_at": "2026-09-17T14:41:18Z",
